WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
This is how to create single word captions in Premiere Pro.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.680
Start by heading to the Workspaces options and selecting Captions and Graphics.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.240
Come up to Text, make sure your audio is selected and then choose Transcribe.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.080
Premiere will transcribe your audio and generate the transcript.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.880
Check that everything is correct, then click the CC button.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.920
This will open up this window.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:28.560
Under Layout, click Single Word and then click Create Captions.

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.760
And now you have single word captions in your video.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.160
To customise your text, select all the captions, head to the Properties panel,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.240
where you'll find controls for the Transform, Font, Size and Colour.
